                                english: "1. A chemical reaction has taken place if there is a change in state, change in colour, evolution of a gas, or change in temperature.\n\n2. Word-equation: Magnesium + Oxygen → Magnesium oxide.\n\n3. Reactants: Substances that undergo chemical change (LHS). Products: New substances formed (RHS).\n\n4. Skeletal chemical equation: Unbalanced equation with chemical formulae. E.g., Mg + O₂ → MgO.\n\n5. Law of conservation of mass: Mass can neither be created nor destroyed in a chemical reaction. Number of atoms of each element must be equal on both sides.\n\n6. Balancing steps: (i) Draw boxes around each formula, (ii) List number of atoms of elements, (iii) Start with compound containing maximum atoms, (iv) Balance one element at a time, (v) Check correctness.\n\n7. Example: Fe + H₂O → Fe₃O₄ + H₂. Balanced: 3Fe + 4H₂O → Fe₃O₄ + 4H₂.\n\n8. Physical states: (g) gas, (l) liquid, (aq) aqueous solution, (s) solid. Example: 3Fe(s) + 4H₂O(g) → Fe₃O₄(s) + 4H₂(g).\n\n9. Reaction conditions (temperature, pressure, catalyst) are indicated above/below the arrow.",
                                hindi: "1. Chemical reaction हुआ है यदि state में change, colour में change, gas का evolution, या temperature में change हो।\n\n2. Word-equation: Magnesium + Oxygen → Magnesium oxide.\n\n3. Reactants: वे substances जो chemical change से गुजरते हैं (LHS). Products: बनने वाले नए substances (RHS).\n\n4. Skeletal chemical equation: Chemical formulae के साथ unbalanced equation. जैसे Mg + O₂ → MgO.\n\n5. Law of conservation of mass: Chemical reaction में mass न तो create हो सकता है न destroy. दोनों sides पर प्रत्येक element के atoms की संख्या equal होनी चाहिए.\n\n6. Balancing steps: (i) प्रत्येक formula के around boxes बनाएँ, (ii) Elements के atoms की संख्या list करें, (iii) Maximum atoms वाले compound से शुरू करें, (iv) एक-एक element balance करें, (v) Correctness check करें.\n\n7. Example: Fe + H₂O → Fe₃O₄ + H₂. Balanced: 3Fe + 4H₂O → Fe₃O₄ + 4H₂.\n\n8. Physical states: (g) gas, (l) liquid, (aq) aqueous solution, (s) solid. Example: 3Fe(s) + 4H₂O(g) → Fe₃O₄(s) + 4H₂(g).\n\n9. Reaction conditions (temperature, pressure, catalyst) arrow के ऊपर/नीचे indicate किए जाते हैं.\nKeywords: chemical equation, skeletal equation, balancing, law of conservation of mass, reactants, products, physical states"
