                                english: "1. Combination reaction: Two or more reactants combine to form a single product. E.g., CaO(s) + H₂O(l) → Ca(OH)₂(aq) + Heat.\n\n2. Exothermic reactions: Heat is released along with products. E.g., burning of coal: C(s) + O₂(g) → CO₂(g).\n\n3. Respiration is an exothermic process: C₆H₁₂O₆(aq) + 6O₂(aq) → 6CO₂(aq) + 6H₂O(l) + energy.\n\n4. Decomposition reaction: A single reactant breaks down to give simpler products. Requires energy (heat, light, or electricity).\n\n5. Thermal decomposition: CaCO₃(s) → CaO(s) + CO₂(g) (on heating).\n\n6. Electrolytic decomposition: 2H₂O(l) → 2H₂(g) + O₂(g) (electricity).\n\n7. Photolytic decomposition: 2AgCl(s) → 2Ag(s) + Cl₂(g) (sunlight). Used in black and white photography.\n\n8. Endothermic reactions: Energy is absorbed. E.g., Ba(OH)₂ + NH₄Cl → reaction feels cold.\n\n9. Displacement reaction: More reactive metal displaces less reactive metal from its salt solution. E.g., Fe(s) + CuSO₄(aq) → FeSO₄(aq) + Cu(s).\n\n10. Double displacement reaction: Exchange of ions between reactants. E.g., Na₂SO₄(aq) + BaCl₂(aq) → BaSO₄(s) + 2NaCl(aq). Precipitate formed.\n\n11. Oxidation: Substance gains oxygen. Reduction: Substance loses oxygen. Redox reactions: One reactant gets oxidised, other gets reduced. E.g., CuO + H₂ → Cu + H₂O.\n\n12. Corrosion: Metal attacked by moisture, acids, etc. (e.g., rusting of iron, black coating on silver, green coating on copper).\n\n13. Rancidity: Fats and oils get oxidised, smell and taste change. Antioxidants added to prevent; nitrogen flushing in chips packets.",
                                hindi: "1. Combination reaction: दो या अधिक reactants combine होकर single product बनाते हैं. जैसे CaO(s) + H₂O(l) → Ca(OH)₂(aq) + Heat.\n\n2. Exothermic reactions: Products के साथ heat release होती है. जैसे burning of coal: C(s) + O₂(g) → CO₂(g).\n\n3. Respiration एक exothermic process है: C₆H₁₂O₆(aq) + 6O₂(aq) → 6CO₂(aq) + 6H₂O(l) + energy.\n\n4. Decomposition reaction: Single reactant टूटकर simpler products बनाता है. Energy (heat, light, या electricity) चाहिए.\n\n5. Thermal decomposition: CaCO₃(s) → CaO(s) + CO₂(g) (heating पर).\n\n6. Electrolytic decomposition: 2H₂O(l) → 2H₂(g) + O₂(g) (electricity).\n\n7. Photolytic decomposition: 2AgCl(s) → 2Ag(s) + Cl₂(g) (sunlight). Black and white photography में उपयोग.\n\n8. Endothermic reactions: Energy absorb होती है. जैसे Ba(OH)₂ + NH₄Cl → reaction ठंडा महसूस होता है.\n\n9. Displacement reaction: ज्यादा reactive metal कम reactive metal को उसके salt solution से displace करता है. जैसे Fe(s) + CuSO₄(aq) → FeSO₄(aq) + Cu(s).\n\n10. Double displacement reaction: Reactants के बीच ions का exchange. जैसे Na₂SO₄(aq) + BaCl₂(aq) → BaSO₄(s) + 2NaCl(aq). Precipitate बनता है.\n\n11. Oxidation: Substance oxygen gain करता है. Reduction: Substance oxygen lose करता है. Redox reactions: एक reactant oxidise होता है, दूसरा reduce होता है. जैसे CuO + H₂ → Cu + H₂O.\n\n12. Corrosion: Metal moisture, acids, etc. से attack होता है (जैसे iron की rusting, silver पर black coating, copper पर green coating).\n\n13. Rancidity: Fats और oils oxidise हो जाते हैं, smell और taste बदल जाते हैं. Antioxidants add किए जाते हैं; chips packets में nitrogen flushing.\nKeywords: combination reaction, exothermic, decomposition, thermal decomposition, electrolytic, photolytic, endothermic, displacement, double displacement, oxidation, reduction, redox, corrosion, rancidity"
