                            display_name: {
                                english: "Properties, Reactivity Series & Ionic Compounds",
                                hindi: "Properties, Reactivity Series और Ionic Compounds"
                            },
                            description: {
                                english: "1. Metals: Lustrous, hard, malleable, ductile, good conductors of heat and electricity, sonorous. Except mercury (liquid).\n\n2. Non-metals: Not malleable/ductile, poor conductors (except graphite), solids or gases (except bromine-liquid).\n\n3. Exceptions: Gallium and caesium have low melting points (melt on palm). Iodine is lustrous. Diamond (carbon allotrope) is hardest natural substance. Graphite conducts electricity. Alkali metals (Li, Na, K) are soft, low density, low melting point.\n\n4. Metal + Oxygen → Metal oxide (basic). E.g., 2Cu + O₂ → 2CuO.\n\n5. Amphoteric oxides: React with both acids and bases. E.g., Al₂O₃, ZnO. Al₂O₃ + 6HCl → 2AlCl₃ + 3H₂O; Al₂O₃ + 2NaOH → 2NaAlO₂ + H₂O.\n\n6. Metal + Water → Metal oxide/hydroxide + Hydrogen. K, Na react violently with cold water; Ca less violent; Mg with hot water; Al, Fe, Zn with steam; Pb, Cu, Ag, Au do not react.\n\n7. Metal + Dilute acid → Salt + Hydrogen. Reactivity: Mg > Al > Zn > Fe > Pb > Cu. HNO₃ is strong oxidising agent (does not give H₂ generally). Aqua regia (3:1 HCl:HNO₃) dissolves gold.\n\n8. Displacement reactions: More reactive metal displaces less reactive metal from salt solution. E.g., Fe + CuSO₄ → FeSO₄ + Cu.\n\n9. Reactivity series (decreasing): K > Na > Ca > Mg > Al > Zn > Fe > Pb > [H] > Cu > Hg > Ag > Au.\n\n10. Ionic compounds: Formed by transfer of electrons from metal to non-metal. Cations (+) and anions (-). E.g., NaCl (Na⁺Cl⁻), MgCl₂ (Mg²⁺ 2Cl⁻).\n\n11. Properties of ionic compounds: Solids, hard, brittle, high melting/boiling points, soluble in water, insoluble in kerosene/petrol. Conduct electricity in molten state or aqueous solution (ions free to move), not in solid state.\n\n12. Occurrence of metals: Minerals (elements/compounds in earth's crust), ores (minerals with high metal percentage).\n\n13. Extraction: (i) Low reactivity metals (Au, Ag, Pt, Cu) found free; (ii) Medium reactivity (Zn, Fe, Pb) as oxides, sulphides, carbonates — roasting (sulphide → oxide), calcination (carbonate → oxide), reduction with carbon; (iii) High reactivity (K, Na, Ca, Mg, Al) — electrolytic reduction.\n\n14. Thermit reaction: Fe₂O₃ + 2Al → 2Fe + Al₂O₃ + Heat. Used to join railway tracks.\n\n15. Refining: Electrolytic refining (impure metal anode, pure metal cathode, metal salt electrolyte).\n\n16. Corrosion: Silver → black (Ag₂S); Copper → green (basic copper carbonate); Iron → rust (Fe₂O₃·xH₂O).\n\n17. Prevention: Painting, oiling, greasing, galvanising (zinc coating), chrome plating, anodising, alloying.\n\n18. Alloys: Homogeneous mixture of two or more metals or metal + non-metal. E.g., Steel (Fe + C), Stainless steel (Fe + Ni + Cr), Brass (Cu + Zn), Bronze (Cu + Sn), Solder (Pb + Sn), Amalgam (with mercury).",
                                hindi: "1. Metals: Lustrous, hard, malleable, ductile, heat और electricity के good conductors, sonorous. Mercury को छोड़कर (liquid).\n\n2. Non-metals: Malleable/ductile नहीं, poor conductors (graphite को छोड़कर), solids या gases (bromine-liquid को छोड़कर).\n\n3. Exceptions: Gallium और caesium के low melting points (palm पर melt). Iodine lustrous. Diamond (carbon allotrope) hardest natural substance. Graphite electricity conduct करता है. Alkali metals (Li, Na, K) soft, low density, low melting point.\n\n4. Metal + Oxygen → Metal oxide (basic). जैसे 2Cu + O₂ → 2CuO.\n\n5. Amphoteric oxides: Acids और bases दोनों के साथ react. जैसे Al₂O₃, ZnO. Al₂O₃ + 6HCl → 2AlCl₃ + 3H₂O; Al₂O₃ + 2NaOH → 2NaAlO₂ + H₂O.\n\n6. Metal + Water → Metal oxide/hydroxide + Hydrogen. K, Na cold water से violently react; Ca less violent; Mg hot water से; Al, Fe, Zn steam से; Pb, Cu, Ag, Au react नहीं करते.\n\n7. Metal + Dilute acid → Salt + Hydrogen. Reactivity: Mg > Al > Zn > Fe > Pb > Cu. HNO₃ strong oxidising agent (H₂ generally नहीं देता). Aqua regia (3:1 HCl:HNO₃) gold dissolve करता है.\n\n8. Displacement reactions: ज्यादा reactive metal कम reactive metal को salt solution से displace करता है. जैसे Fe + CuSO₄ → FeSO₄ + Cu.\n\n9. Reactivity series (decreasing): K > Na > Ca > Mg > Al > Zn > Fe > Pb > [H] > Cu > Hg > Ag > Au.\n\n10. Ionic compounds: Metal से non-metal में electrons transfer से बनते हैं. Cations (+) और anions (-). जैसे NaCl (Na⁺Cl⁻), MgCl₂ (Mg²⁺ 2Cl⁻).\n\n11. Ionic compounds के properties: Solids, hard, brittle, high melting/boiling points, water में soluble, kerosene/petrol में insoluble. Molten state या aqueous solution में electricity conduct (ions free to move), solid state में नहीं.\n\n12. Metals की occurrence: Minerals (earth's crust में elements/compounds), ores (high metal percentage वाले minerals).\n\n13. Extraction: (i) Low reactivity metals (Au, Ag, Pt, Cu) free में मिलते हैं; (ii) Medium reactivity (Zn, Fe, Pb) oxides, sulphides, carbonates के रूप में — roasting (sulphide → oxide), calcination (carbonate → oxide), carbon से reduction; (iii) High reactivity (K, Na, Ca, Mg, Al) — electrolytic reduction.\n\n14. Thermit reaction: Fe₂O₃ + 2Al → 2Fe + Al₂O₃ + Heat. Railway tracks join करने में उपयोग.\n\n15. Refining: Electrolytic refining (impure metal anode, pure metal cathode, metal salt electrolyte).\n\n16. Corrosion: Silver → black (Ag₂S); Copper → green (basic copper carbonate); Iron → rust (Fe₂O₃·xH₂O).\n\n17. Prevention: Painting, oiling, greasing, galvanising (zinc coating), chrome plating, anodising, alloying.\n\n18. Alloys: दो या अधिक metals या metal + non-metal का homogeneous mixture. जैसे Steel (Fe + C), Stainless steel (Fe + Ni + Cr), Brass (Cu + Zn), Bronze (Cu + Sn), Solder (Pb + Sn), Amalgam (mercury के साथ).\nKeywords: metals, non-metals, malleability, ductility, sonorous, amphoteric oxides, reactivity series, displacement reaction, ionic compounds, roasting, calcination, thermit reaction, electrolytic refining, corrosion, galvanisation, alloys"
                            },
