                        {
                            id: "sci10_c8",
                            display_name: {
                                english: "Sexual Reproduction in Plants & Humans",
                                hindi: "Plants और Humans में Sexual Reproduction"
                            },
                            description: {
                                english: "1. Sexual reproduction involves two parents. DNA from two individuals combines.\n\n2. Meiosis: Special cell division in specialised organs producing germ-cells with half the number of chromosomes and half the DNA. When germ-cells from two individuals combine, chromosome number and DNA content are re-established.\n\n3. Male gamete: Motile, smaller. Female gamete: Contains stored food, larger.\n\n4. Flower parts: Sepals (protect bud), Petals (attract pollinators), Stamens (male: anther + filament), Pistil (female: stigma + style + ovary).\n\n5. Unisexual flowers (papaya, watermelon) contain either stamens or pistil. Bisexual flowers (Hibiscus, mustard) contain both.\n\n6. Pollination: Transfer of pollen from stamen to stigma. Self-pollination (same flower) or cross-pollination (different flower). Agents: wind, water, animals.\n\n7. Fertilisation: Pollen tube grows from pollen grain through style to ovary. Male germ-cell fuses with female gamete → zygote.\n\n8. Post-fertilisation: Zygote divides to form embryo within ovule. Ovule develops tough coat → seed. Ovary grows and ripens → fruit. Petals, sepals, stamens, style, stigma may shrivel and fall off.\n\n9. Germination: Seed contains future plant (embryo) which develops into seedling under appropriate conditions.\n\n10. Human male reproductive system: Testes (produce sperms, located in scrotum outside abdominal cavity for lower temperature), vas deferens, urethra (common passage for sperms and urine), prostate gland and seminal vesicles (add secretions for transport and nutrition), penis.\n\n11. Human female reproductive system: Ovaries (produce eggs and hormones), oviducts (fallopian tubes), uterus, cervix, vagina.\n\n12. Puberty changes: Common to both — thick hair in armpits and genital area, thinner hair on legs/arms/face, oily skin, pimples. Girls — breast size increases, menstruation begins. Boys — facial hair, voice cracks, penis enlarges and becomes erect.\n\n13. Menstruation: If egg is not fertilised, it lives for about one day. Uterine lining breaks and comes out through vagina as blood and mucous. Cycle takes place roughly every month, lasts 2-8 days.\n\n14. Placenta: Disc embedded in uterine wall. Contains villi on embryo's side, blood spaces on mother's side. Provides large surface area for glucose and oxygen to pass from mother to embryo. Waste removed by transferring into mother's blood.\n\n15. Contraception methods: Barrier (condoms), hormonal (oral pills), IUDs (copper-T), surgical (vas deferens/fallopian tube blocking).\n\n16. STIs: Gonorrhoea, syphilis (bacterial), warts, HIV-AIDS (viral). Condoms prevent transmission to some extent.",
                                hindi: "1. Sexual reproduction में two parents involve होते हैं. दो individuals का DNA combine होता है.\n\n2. Meiosis: Specialised organs में special cell division जो germ-cells को half chromosomes और half DNA के साथ produce करती है. जब दो individuals के germ-cells combine होते हैं, chromosome number और DNA content re-established होते हैं.\n\n3. Male gamete: Motile, smaller. Female gamete: Stored food contain, larger.\n\n4. Flower parts: Sepals (bud protect), Petals (pollinators attract), Stamens (male: anther + filament), Pistil (female: stigma + style + ovary).\n\n5. Unisexual flowers (papaya, watermelon) में either stamens या pistil होते हैं. Bisexual flowers (Hibiscus, mustard) में दोनों होते हैं.\n\n6. Pollination: Stamen से stigma तक pollen का transfer. Self-pollination (same flower) या cross-pollination (different flower). Agents: wind, water, animals.\n\n7. Fertilisation: Pollen tube pollen grain से style के through ovary तक grow करता है. Male germ-cell female gamete से fuse → zygote.\n\n8. Post-fertilisation: Zygote divide होकर ovule में embryo form करता है. Ovule tough coat develop → seed. Ovary grow और ripen → fruit. Petals, sepals, stamens, style, stigma shrivel और fall हो सकते हैं.\n\n9. Germination: Seed में future plant (embryo) होता है जो appropriate conditions में seedling में develop होता है.\n\n10. Human male reproductive system: Testes (sperms produce, lower temperature के लिए scrotum में abdominal cavity के बाहर), vas deferens, urethra (sperms और urine के लिए common passage), prostate gland और seminal vesicles (transport और nutrition के लिए secretions add), penis.\n\n11. Human female reproductive system: Ovaries (eggs और hormones produce), oviducts (fallopian tubes), uterus, cervix, vagina.\n\n12. Puberty changes: दोनों के लिए common — armpits और genital area में thick hair, legs/arms/face पर thinner hair, oily skin, pimples. Girls — breast size increases, menstruation शुरू. Boys — facial hair, voice cracks, penis enlarges और erect होता है.\n\n13. Menstruation: अगर egg fertilised नहीं होता, तो लगभग एक दिन जीवित रहता है. Uterine lining break होकर vagina से blood और mucous के रूप में बाहर आती है. Cycle लगभग हर महीने होता है, 2-8 दिन lasts.\n\n14. Placenta: Uterine wall में embedded disc. Embryo की side पर villi, mother की side पर blood spaces. Glucose और oxygen mother से embryo तक pass होने के लिए large surface area provide करता है. Waste mother के blood में transfer करके remove होता है.\n\n15. Contraception methods: Barrier (condoms), hormonal (oral pills), IUDs (copper-T), surgical (vas deferens/fallopian tube blocking).\n\n16. STIs: Gonorrhoea, syphilis (bacterial), warts, HIV-AIDS (viral). Condoms कुछ हद तक transmission prevent करते हैं.\nKeywords: sexual reproduction, meiosis, gametes, flower parts, pollination, fertilisation, zygote, seed, fruit, human reproductive system, puberty, menstruation, placenta, contraception, STIs"
                            },
                            diagrams: null
                        }
